WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.820
Change evidence explains the path from request to closure.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:23.080
Useful evidence can include change tickets, approvals, implementation notes, test results, configuration records, screenshots at a high level, pull requests, deployment logs, scan results, monitoring records, and updated diagrams, inventories, or control narratives.

3
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:28.700
Not every change needs every artifact, but meaningful changes should leave a reviewable trail.

4
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:35.380
Evidence should be current, traceable, reviewable, and consistent with the live system.

5
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.800
Current evidence reflects what actually happened.

6
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:43.980
Traceable evidence connects the change to affected systems, owners, approvals, and controls.

7
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:52.560
Reviewable evidence can be understood by assessors, security teams, engineers, operations teams, and compliance teams.

8
00:00:52.660 --> 00:01:00.500
Consistency means tickets, diagrams, inventories, control narratives, and deployment records tell the same story.

9
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:07.580
Documentation updates are often the difference between a successful technical change and a sustainable security program.

10
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:19.040
If a change modifies architecture, dependencies, data flows, control implementation, monitoring coverage, or customer responsibility, the related documentation may need to change.

11
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:25.220
Otherwise, the next assessment or incident response effort will be based on outdated assumptions.

12
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.160
Documentation drift is a common source of review friction.

13
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:34.640
Undocumented production changes are risky because they bypass the evidence chain.

14
00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:43.300
They make it harder to explain what changed, why it changed, whether it was approved, whether it was tested, and whether it affected security posture.

15
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.720
Strong programs make the approved path the practical path.

16
00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:53.020
The evidence process should be light enough to use and strong enough to support trust.
